{
  "slug": "mtw-e2e-runner",
  "name": "Mtw E2e Runner",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "JSON-driven E2E browser test runner — no JavaScript test files needed. Define tests as JSON action arrays and run\nthem in parallel against a Chrome pool (browserless/chrome). Includes 3 specialized agents (test-creator,\ntest-analyzer, test-improver), 4 slash commands (/run, /create-test, /verify-issue, /capture), and 16 MCP tools for\nthe full test lifecycle. Features 28+ built-in actions, AI-powered visual verification, network request debugging,\nflaky test detection with stability learning, reusable parameterized modules, project variables, and a real-time\nweb dashboard.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, **3 agents**, **4 commands** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `e2e-testing` (Create, run, and debug JSON-driven E2E browser tests with Chrome pool integration)\n- **Agents** (3): `test-analyzer` (Use this agent to diagnose E2E test failures, analyze flaky tests, investigate network errors, and provide stability insights), `test-creator` (Use this agent to create new E2E tests by exploring the application UI, analyzing source code, and designing…), `test-improver` (Use this agent to improve existing E2E tests — refactor verbose evaluate actions into built-in alternatives, extract duplicated…)\n- **Commands** (4): `capture` (Capture a screenshot of any URL with automatic authentication), `create-test` (Create a new E2E test by exploring the UI and designing test actions), `run` (Run E2E tests and analyze results with screenshots and network drill-down), `verify-issue` (Verify a GitHub/GitLab issue by creating and running E2E tests)\n- **MCP servers** (1): `e2e-runner`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install mtw-e2e-runner@claude-community` from `fastslack/mtw-e2e-runner`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 1,
    "agent": 3,
    "command": 4,
    "mcp": 1
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
  "author": {
    "name": "Matware"
  },
